# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore rules for the MUSA app-service repository.
# Principle: anything large, derived or machine-specific stays on disk only.
# git never forgets a binary, so the decision has to be made before the add.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Derived / tooling state ---------------------------------------------
# Codebase Memory MCP local index; rebuildable with index_repository.
.codebase-memory/

# Reasonix task/session state (events.jsonl, snapshots, task locks). It is local
# to one machine and churns on every tool call, so it is not project content.
# The extension's configuration is reasonix.toml, which IS tracked.
.reasonix/

# Python bytecode, e.g. from a test that imports a checker in tools/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
build/
_build/

# --- Scratch / pre-selection material -------------------------------------
# Downloads, shortlists and dead ends, e.g. the marketing image pre-selection
# in scratch/marketing_images/. Nothing under scratch/ is referenced by
# source/, so it must not pad every clone.
scratch/

# --- Local editor / agent configuration -----------------------------------
# Deliberately TRACKED, not ignored. .claude/, .cursor/, .vscode/ and .zed/
# hold this project's agent rules and MCP setup, which the team needs; ignoring
# them would also silently skip NEW files placed in those folders.
# Caveat: the MCP configs embed a machine-specific absolute path such as
# c:\Users\<user>\...\codebase-memory-mcp.exe, so a collaborator may have to
# adjust theirs. If that becomes a real problem, version a .dist template
# instead of ignoring the folder.

# --- 3D models are TRACKED (deliberate reversal, 2026-09-18) --------------
# The `*.glb` rule was removed so the four models in source/assets/models/
# (~29.6 MB) ship with the repository. Reason: docs/adr/0005 publishes
# `source/` to GitHub Pages and the WebGL viewers fetch the models over http.
# There is no object store yet and 29.6 MB is cheaper than standing one up for
# a demo. This knowingly breaks invariant 3 of docs/HANDOFF.md §5 ("zero
# binário grande versionado") -- see the note under §5 and the item in §11.
# To revert: restore the rule, move the models to a bucket and keep only the
# URL in the ficha. Note that tools/fetch_models.py skips any file already
# present at the exact expected size, so a Pages build with the models
# committed stays green (it reports "skip <name> (already present)").

# --- The hero montage stays out of git ------------------------------------
# source/assets/video/Musa_montage_02_web.mp4 (4.3 MB) is referenced by NO
# markup any more, and its video track is HEVC/H.265 -- a codec no browser
# decodes, so it reports readyState 4 and paints nothing (HANDOFF §7).
# Versioning 4.3 MB of an unplayable, unreferenced blob is pure history weight.
# Transcode to H.264/AVC before tracking it again.
source/assets/video/Musa_montage_02_web.mp4

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ---------------------------------------------
# .git/    Not a worktree path: it IS the repository. Git never tracks paths
#          inside .git/, so a rule here is a no-op. Its size is HISTORY, and
#          history only shrinks by rewriting it or by keeping big binaries out
#          in the first place -- which is what the *.glb rule above is for.
# .github/ Holds the CI workflows and .github/copilot-instructions.md. GitHub
#          reads those from the REMOTE, so ignoring them would silently break
#          CI and strip the project agent rules from every collaborator.

# --- OS artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.egg-info/
